---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { docsGroups } from '../../../data/docs';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Start with Meridian"
  description="A guided introduction to the engine, the repository, and the systems taking shape inside it."
  currentPath="/meridian/docs"
  home
>
  <header class="docs-home-hero">
    <p class="kicker"><span>Meridian documentation</span></p>
    <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">Start with Meridian.</h1>
    <p>Meridian is a Rust engine and one integrated creator application, planned for an open-source release under MIT or Apache-2.0. These guides explain what exists and how the pieces fit together while the source remains private during early development.</p>
    <div class="inline-actions">
      <a class="action action-primary" href="/meridian/docs/learn/what-is-meridian">Understand the engine <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      <a class="action" href="/meridian/docs/build/from-source">Preview the source workflow <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="docs-introduction">
    <p class="section-number">Choose a way in</p>
    <h2>You do not need to read the repository in directory order.</h2>
    <p>Start with the question you have. The documentation is organized for people learning the architecture, developers working with the source, readers exploring named systems, and anyone looking for the authoritative record.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="docs-group-grid">
    {docsGroups.map((group, index) => (
      <section>
        <span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
        <h2>{group.label}</h2>
        <p>{group.description}</p>
        <ul>{group.items.map((item) => <li><a href={item.href}>{item.label} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>)}</ul>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <aside class="docs-authority-note">
    <strong>The website explains. The repository decides.</strong>
    <p>Versioned specifications, typed registries, architecture decisions, and current evidence remain authoritative inside the private source. The website describes that record without exposing the repository before release.</p>
    <a class="text-action" href="/meridian/docs/reference/specifications">Find the owning source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </aside>
</DocsLayout>
